      bodyEn: "The word 茶 (chá) conquered the world via two routes. Sea (Fujian, \"te\") → tea/thé/Tee. Land (Mandarin, \"cha\") → chai/çay.\n\nIn China, tea is classified by color:\n\n- 绿茶 (green, Zhejiang)\n- 红茶 (red = \"black tea\" in the West)\n- 乌龙茶 (oolong, semi-fermented)\n- 普洱茶 (pu'er, fermented, Yunnan)\n\nNo sugar, no milk — Chinese tea is drunk pure.",
